```
===================================================================
Detection Name: LSASS Memory Access & Credential Dumping
Author: SOC Team
Data Source: index=edr_sysmon (Sysmon Operational Event Logs)
Event ID: 10 (ProcessAccess)
Target Image: *\lsass.exe
Granted Access Masks:
  - 0x1010 (PROCESS_VM_READ | PROCESS_QUERY_LIMITED_INFORMATION)
  - 0x1410 (PROCESS_VM_READ | PROCESS_QUERY_INFORMATION)
  - 0x1fffff (PROCESS_ALL_ACCESS)
MITRE ATT&CK: T1003 (OS Credential Dumping: LSASS Memory)
Severity: Critical
Common Attacker Tools: 
  - rundll32.exe comsvcs.dll, MiniDump
  - procdump.exe
  - mimikatz.exe / sekurlsa::logonpasswords
Recommended Action:
  1. Immediately isolate host from network via EDR/firewall.
  2. Terminate attacking source process (SourceImage / PID).
  3. Assume all cached credentials on the asset are compromised.
  4. Initiate enterprise credential rotation and Kerberos TGT purge.
===================================================================
```
index=edr_sysmon EventCode=10 TargetImage="*\\lsass.exe" GrantedAccess IN ("0x1010", "0x1410", "0x1fffff")
| eval Attacking_Process=SourceImage
| eval Target=TargetImage
| table _time, host, SourceImage, TargetImage, GrantedAccess, CallTrace
| sort - _time
